Package: kaaryasoochi
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: iproute2, libnotify-bin, systemd
Description: schedule and manage cron-style jobs
 Kaaryasoochi schedules commands and scripts the way cron does, with a desktop
 window (WebKitGTK) to create jobs, pick schedules and read each run's output:
 one-shot, interval and crontab schedules, run history, retries, timeouts,
 per-job time zones and catch-up of runs missed while the machine was off.
 .
 Jobs are run by a per-user systemd user service (kaaryasoochi-server), as
 that user and never as root. The kaaryasoochi launcher enables it on first
 launch; it is not enabled for every user at install time.
